-- --opens specification (seg/WRITING.md, rule 6) for the classification of
-- pointed simply connected 3-types (doc/postnikov-classification.pdf):
-- ClassAb, ClassBase, ClassEM, ClassFib, ClassPost, PostnikovClassification, and
-- Pi3Classified (pi3 S2 = Z through the classification; rep opens realise: rep-fib
-- is the statement at realise t by definition).
-- One entry per declaration, generated from --opened (28 Oct 2026) and read
-- against the note module by module (not a line-by-line textual audit).
-- Kinds of openings:
--   types and accessors: PtEquiv, PtMap, PtSec, Equiv, isEquiv, isConn,
--     isTrunc, the Sigma/record accessors of each module (Acs, R, St, ..);
--   numeral spellings: two, three, four, five against the suc-spellings of
--     EM.Stage and KK (K2, K3 unfold to EMn.Kstage; KK.K/KK.pt to EMSpace);
--   by-definition steps of the text: K(B,4) = Tor K(B,3) (EM.Step.next,
--     Deloop.Torsors.Tor, Deloop.ptT); K(A,2) = (Kstage 0).X; the value of
--     the chain at (A, B, k) in PostnikovClassification.Agree.pe (compose,
--     sigma-equiv, the steps e01..e34, alpha); pi_n (K_n B) carrier and
--     addition (O3, O2ab, PiOne.O, comp);
--   ClassEM.Band2.fun-def (refl): comparing (KK.e 0).1.1 with EMSpace.loop0.1
--     opens the band (EM1.band, TrivG.kb/tb, TorId.AutM.fa,
--     Trunc.induction): a checker unfolding inside a by-definition step,
--     isolated in this one refl lemma (rule 4).
